PHP execution is provided by Sean Morris and the contributors to
https://github.com/seanmorris/php-wasm . This project consumes their published
runtime and extension packages. Their copyright, licenses and notices are
preserved with the distributed assets.

The PHP and MariaDB WebAssembly builds rely on Emscripten, maintained by the
contributors to https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten .

MariaDB integration is provided by https://github.com/joomengine/mariadb-wasm-bridge
and its separately maintained database dependency https://github.com/shyim/lite4mariadb .
MariaDB and lite4mariadb retain their upstream licenses and source provenance.

Joomla is provided by https://github.com/joomla/joomla-cms and retains its GNU
General Public License and all notices included in its release packages. The
reviewed browser database-configuration adapter verifies the original model and
console-command source hashes, preserves their GPL headers, and retains the
original behavior on conventional PHP. Its exact source inventory and scope are
documented in dependencies/joomla/README.md.

Joomla Component Builder is provided by Llewellyn van der Merwe and Vast
Development Method through https://github.com/joomengine/pkg-component-builder .
Its GPL-2.0-or-later license and copyright notices remain in the derived browser
packages. The reviewed reader-interface adjustment preserves its source header.
The upstream fixture license is included at test/fixtures/LICENSE.jcb.txt.
JCB's original sponsor banner artwork is included unchanged from the pinned
https://github.com/vdm-io/jcb-external source. The artwork remains credited to
its respective creators; sponsor destinations and visible references are retained.
Asset checksums, source URLs and the reviewed magazine image reference correction
are recorded in dependencies/jcb-banners/assets.json and package provenance.

JCB spreadsheet support builds on PHPOffice/PhpSpreadsheet and ZipStream-PHP,
with Composer PCRE, Mark Baker's Complex and Matrix libraries, MyCLabs PHP Enum,
and PHP-FIG HTTP Message and Simple Cache interfaces. Their MIT licenses are
retained in the composed vendor tree. Four reviewed XLS/OLE packing constants
use signed integer equivalents to preserve their bytes on 32-bit PHP. A numeric
range check preserves floating-point values outside the integer range before
casting. Original and adjusted source hashes are recorded without changing
upstream notices.
Exact source URLs, versions, archive
checksums and license declarations are recorded in
dependencies/jcb-spreadsheet/packages.json and each derived package's provenance.
Composer is provided by https://github.com/composer/composer under the MIT
license; its version and verified binary checksum are recorded in that provenance.

The playground source license does not replace the licenses of these bundled
dependencies. The static distribution includes their notices and source links.

The loadable fileinfo extensions are compiled from the pinned official PHP
sources and include libmagic. Their PHP and libmagic licenses and compiled-source
copyright notices are distributed beside each module, with source checksums and
build provenance.

The loadable cURL extensions use PHP's unchanged ext/curl and Sean Morris's
https://github.com/seanmorris/php-wasm-curl implementation of libcurl over Fetch,
revision 6085917954da9682c32ebcbea27a626d2308381b. php-wasm-curl is copyright 2026
Sean Morris, offered under Apache-2.0 or GPL-2.0-only. Its vendored curl 8.22.0 public
headers are copyright 1996-2026 Daniel Stenberg and contributors under the curl
license. PHP's license and the implementation's LICENSE, LICENSE-GPL, NOTICE,
and COPYING.curl notices accompany the compiled modules and their provenance.

The Sodium modules compile PHP's ext/sodium against the official libsodium
1.0.22-RELEASE sources from https://github.com/jedisct1/libsodium . The libsodium
contributors' ISC license and the matching PHP license are shipped beside each
module. The verified source archive digest, source inventories, compiler identity,
and binary digest are recorded in the module's build provenance.

The published php-cgi-wasm 0.2.0 JavaScript CGI adapter is supplied by Sean Morris
and contributors under its preserved Apache-2.0 license. JoomEngine applies a
reviewed request-input correction to breakoutRequest.mjs, PhpCgiBase.mjs, and
PhpCgiWebBase.mjs: bounded byte decoding and indexed input reads preserve binary
request bodies without repeated array shifts. The PHP WebAssembly binary is not
modified. scripts/cgi-request-overlay.mjs verifies each original source digest;
the generated manifest records both original and adjusted source digests.

The JoomEngine MCP package is provided by Llewellyn van der Merwe and Vast
Development Method through https://github.com/joomengine/mcp_package . Version 1.0.10 and its bundled
component and plugins retain their GNU GPL version 3 or later notices. Its pinned
package URL and digest are recorded in deploys/jcb-mcp.json. The playground's
private native read diagnostic does not modify the installed package's license,
authentication requirements, or CLI transport guards.

Service Directory is provided by Lemuel van der Merwe and Vast Development Method
through https://github.com/joomengine/pkg-servicedirectory . Its Joomla 5 and
Joomla 6 packages retain the GNU GPL version 2 or later license and copyright
notices included by their authors. Exact package source revisions and digests
are recorded in deploys/servicedirectory.json.

Joomla language packages are derived from the official translation teams' sources
at https://github.com/joomla/core-translations under GNU GPL version 2 or later.
Their translations, manifests, localise classes, update identities and notices
are preserved. Deterministic assembly completes only empty package version/date
placeholders and builds any declared child archives. The pinned source revision,
archive checksum and resulting file provenance are recorded in
dependencies/joomla-languages/packages.json and the generated package inventories.
